Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy over-corrected toward token-by-token constrained decoding.
// It achieved perfect syntax, but accuracy collapsed because the SQL grammar alone
// is too permissive: many locally valid next tokens lead to globally nonsensical
// queries such as malformed SELECT lists. The failure preview indicates that the
// decoder stayed inside the grammar yet lost LM guidance about which valid SQL
// token best matches the question and schema.
//
// The revised strategy keeps the parser as a hard safety filter but restores much
// stronger LM influence inside the SQL span. Outside the span, we still open `<<`
// aggressively so the answer enters constrained mode quickly. Inside the span, we
// no longer call `ConstrainedStep` blindly. Instead, we ask the parser for a small
// set of top valid candidates under the current LM logits using
// `TopValidCandidates`, strongly boost exactly those valid candidates, penalize EOS
